  "body": "**Stacked on #2112** (rest Adaptive, `mkinney:issue/2031-rest-adaptive`, head 71a7fee47). This PR's own change is its last commit (c234093ee); until #2112 merges the diff against main shows #2112's commits too. Merge #2112 first.\n\n## What changed\n\nTests only (no product code): three pins the M5 review of #2112 found missing.\n\n- **Raster half of the entry proof** - `machining2d::adaptive::rest::tests::the_raster_half_of_the_entry_proof_refuses_on_its_own` (unit test, `crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive/rest/tests.rs`). It hands `Entries` a raster holding a 1 mm pillar that the polygon bound does not hold, then asks for a plunge whose rim would stand 0.2 mm inside the pillar: refused. A plunge clear of the pillar by more than the margin is still proved. Inside the planner the raster comes from the same polygon bound (grown), and the polygon half refuses everything the raster would, so no planner fixture can make the raster refuse on its own. The test therefore works on `Entries` directly.\n  - Mutation-checked: removing `&& self.stock.air(p, p, self.footprint)` from `Entries::proved` turns it red, and so does `footprint: 0.0`.\n- **Load ceiling on the default D/80 measuring grid** - `on_the_default_measuring_grid_the_load_stays_under_its_documented_ceiling` (`crates/motion/tests/rest_adaptive/main.rs`). Optimal x 1.2 (`LOAD_CEILING_D80` in `sim.rs`, with its readings documented), on the climb 3 mm corners and on the conventional 3.5 mm corners with 0.3 mm left.\n- **Corner assertion on a fine grid (D/240)** - `on_a_fine_grid_the_corners_read_within_the_planning_margin`. A 26 x 22 pocket with 3.5 mm corners, cut conventionally with 0.3 mm left. On the measuring stock that is 1680 x 1440 cells, under the 4096-cell cap. It must read within the planner's own margin (optimal x 1.05), and every feed stays in the corners.\n- `sim.rs`: `Sim::on_grid(region, cell)` and `assert_load_within(reading, slack)`. `assert_load_held` is now `assert_load_within(.., LOAD_SLACK)`.\n- `docs/decisions/2113-rest-adaptive-pins.md`.\n\n## Readings (debug, optimal load 14.6% of D)\n\n| Fixture | D/80 | D/120 | D/240 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 60 x 40, 3 mm corners, climb | 14.6% | 13.1% | - |\n| 60 x 40, 3.5 mm corners, conventional, 0.3 mm left | 16.7% | 14.7% | - |\n| 26 x 22, 3.5 mm corners, conventional, 0.3 mm left | 14.6% | - | 12.7% |\n| two bays, 10 mm neck | 15.0% | 15.0% | - |\n\nNo real bug showed up. The D/80 excess is the measuring rim taking in wall in a concave corner: the same paths read lower on finer grids.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: motion suites ok (396 s), app suites ok (213 s).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The three new tests, one by one, plus the two mutations above (each red, then reverted).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Windows/Linux: run on macOS only.\n- The island and neck fixtures on D/240: too large for the cap.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium (worked by issue-worker-high; not escalated)\n\nFixes #2113\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
